~ intro
# Light filters in through a window over a desk (I’ll draw it soon)
do Music.switch("Sunshine")
Clay: You’d think at some point I’d stop falling asleep here.
Clay: Ain’t nothing to do about it...
# Mail comes in through the slot
Clay: What's new from the city, then?
Clay: No photo...
do Music.switch("Silence")
Clay: uuuuuggggggghhhhhhhhh........
do Music.switch("Sunshine")
Clay: It's... fine...
Clay: All that's here is that there was a theft at the bank in town...
Clay: Never can be an easy job, eh? Well. Time to get to it!
=> END

do Music.switch("Nice Day")

~ clover
- How are you?
    Clover: I’m doing rather well.
    Clay: Still selling random junk?
    Clover: HEY.
    Clover: It IS NOT random.
    Clay: Isn’t it? In what way is it NOT random?
    Clover: ...
    # Using => to manually return to the top of the dialogue is messy because of how redundant it is, but it’ll work.  
    => clover
- Where were you two nights ago? [if DialogueVars.talked_to_howard1]
    Clover: Clay.
    Clay: Yes...?
    Clover: Surely you know better than to expect I’ll remember that...
    Clay: That’s fair.
    => clover
-  Do you remember coming across a gold ring? [if DialogueVars.talked_to_seb]
    Clover: Yes, actually. Why?
    Clay: I’m investigating a robbery and I was wondering if they would’ve sold it to you.
    Clover: Well, this was sold to me a while back...
    Clover: I don’t know that it’d be what you’re looking for.
    Clay: ...
    Clay: Just tell me and I’ll decide that.
    Clover: It was a very nice ring.
    Clay: ...
    Clay: Do you happen to remember who sold it to you?
    Clover: What is with you today and asking me to remember things...?
    do Music.switch("Secret Jingle")
    Clover: As far as I remember, it was strange young man with reddish hair.
    [wait=0.5]do Music.switch("Nice Day")
    Clay: Well... That’s not helpful.
    set DialogueVars.talked_to_clover = true
    => clover
- Never mind.
=> END

~ howard
- How are you?
    Howard: Good, business has been decent recently.
    Clay: Even with the theft.
    Howard: Honestly, even better. Insurance paid out quite a bit for that thing.
    Clay: ...
    => howard
- Where were you during the break-in?
    Howard: I was in my room.
    Howard: I ended my day a couple hours before and was relaxing.
    Clay: By relaxing, do you happen to mean sleeping?
    Howard: More or less.
    Clay: By the way...
    Clay: When was this?
    Howard: Well...
    Howard: Yesterday I went over to the city to get a bounty placed.
    Howard: So, it would’ve been the night before.
    Clay: Two nights ago, then?
    Howard: That is correct.
    set DialogueVars.talked_to_howard1 = true
    => howard
- What was stolen?
    Howard: I... [wait=1] don’t know.
    Clay: ...
    Howard: Please understand. There were several cases broken.
    Clay: You know how much harder this is going to make this...?
    Howard: I’m very sorry, but if there’s anything I CAN help with I will.
    => howard
- Is there anything else you think I need to know?
    Howard: Not really...
    Howard: You could go talk to Seb though...
    Clay: Why would I do that?
    Howard: Well, I ju- [next=auto]
    Clay: Before you say anythin’ else, just know that there’s no way I will ever want to talk to that spoiled egg.
    do Music.switch("Secret Jingle")
    Howard: Th-the point is that he works here.
    [wait=0.5]do Music.switch("Nice Day")
    Clay: Seb... [wait=1] has a job?
    Howard: Yes...?
    Clay: Well damn, didn’t think Sebby would ever do somethin’ actually useful.
    set DialogueVars.talked_to_howard2 = true
    => howard
- How was babysitting? [if DialogueVars.talked_to_apple]
    Howard: ...
    Clay: Is there any reason you didn’t tell me this before?
    Howard: Not really...?
    Clay: Then why didn’t you tell me?
    Howard: Joyce doesn’t like it when too much attention is called to it.
    Clay: I am investigating. A CRIME.
    Clay: That doesn’t matter.
    Howard: She’s just busy is all.
    Howard: I watch her when she has too much on her plate to make dinner.
    Howard: It’s not exactly responsible to leave a child without food.
    Clay: Fine. Fine.
    set DialogueVars.talked_to_howard3 = true 
    => howard
- Was it a gold ring? [if DialogueVars.talked_to_seb]
    Howard: YES! That’s what it was!
    Clay: Do you remember anything about it?
    Howard: I remember it was sold to me a while back by Clover.
    Clay: Another step on the fetch quest...
    set DialogueVars.talked_to_howard4 = true
    => howard
- Do you know where Clover got it from? [if DialogueVars.talked_to_howard4]
    if DialogueVars.talked_to_clover == true
        Howard: No?
        Clay: Clover says it was Ryan?
        Howard: Oh.[wait=0.5] Joyce’s ex-husband.[wait=0.5] Strange fella.
        Clay: ...
        Howard: I never did like the guy, but he wa-[next=auto]
        Clay: Maybe you couldn’t tell by my silence, but I don’t know him.
        Howard: ...
        Clay: Well?
        do Music.switch("Secret Jingle")
        Howard: I would’ve thought you knew him. That’s more Joyce’s story to tell, though.
        [wait=0.5]do Music.switch("Nice Day")
        Clay: I guess I have to ask her?
        Howard: That’d be my suggestion.  
        set DialogueVars.talked_to_howard5 = true 
        => howard
    else
        Howard: No?
        Clay: Okay then...
        Clay: I guess I’ll ask him.
        => howard
- Never mind.
=> END

~ joyce
- How are you?
    Joyce: Fine.
    Clay: Anything new?
    Joyce: Nope.
    Clay: ...
    Joyce: I don’t exactly have time for small talk.
    Clay: Got it.
    => joyce
- Where were you two nights ago? [if DialogueVars.talked_to_howard1]
    Joyce: I was at home making dinner for myself and Apple.
    Clay: That’s nice!
    Joyce: I try to make good use of ingredients.
    set DialogueVars.talked_to_joyce1 == true
    => joyce
- Who was Ryan? [if DialogueVars.talked_to_howard5]
    Joyce: First of all...
    Joyce: How did you hear that name?
    Clay: Howard let it slip.
    Joyce: Ugh...
    Joyce: He always runs his mouth.
    Joyce: ...
    Joyce: Ryan was my husband. Roughly two years ago he left.
    Joyce: I know you left for a while, so you weren’t here when he was.
    Joyce: Honestly, I really wish you had been there.
    Joyce: I needed the help.
    Joyce: But I’m here now and he isn’t.
    Clay: ...
    set DialogueVars.talked_to_joyce2 = true
    => joyce
- Are you sure? [if DialogueVars.talked_to_howard3 and DialogueVars.talked_to_joyce1 and DialogueVars.talked_to_joyce2]
    Joyce: What do you mean?
    Clay: Wasn’t Apple at Howard’s?
    Joyce: Yeah, she go-[next=auto]
    Clay: You said you were making dinner for you and Apple.
    Clay: According to Howard, you are usually too busy to make dinner when he watches her.
    Joyce: That, wasn’t the case thi-[next=auto]
    Clay: What was the reason then?
    Clay: Why did you not want her around?
    Joyce: CAN YOU JUST LET ME SPEAK?!?
    Clay: ...
    Clay: Sorry.[wait=0.5] I got caught up in the moment. 
    Clay: I don’t get to do this often.
    Joyce: It’s fine.[wait=0.5] I get it.
    Clay: The point is...
    Clay: Where’s the ring?
    Joyce: What...[wait=1.0] ring...?
    Clay: The ring that Ryan sold.
    Clay: I don’t know why he sold it...[wait=0.5] and I don’t need to...
    Clay: But when you lie to me, don’t have an alibi, and are connected to the seller...
    Clay: I have to put you as the prime suspect.
    Joyce: I didn’t do anything.
    Clay: Please understand.[wait=0.5] I have more than enough reason to search your property.
    Joyce: ...
    Joyce: I’ll at least save you the effort.
    Joyce: Come with me and get it.
    Joyce: Just...[wait=1.5] Keep track of Apple for me?
    Clay: Woah woah woah. You’re getting ahead of yourself here.
    Joyce: ...
    Joyce: What?
    Clay: This is a small town.[wait=0.5] Outside of most jurisdictions.
    Clay: I’m just going to detain you for a bit while I figure out how you need to compensate Howard.
    Joyce: ...
    Joyce: Huh.
    Joyce: Any way I can keep the ring?
    Clay: By paying for it like a normal person!
    Clay: Or talk with Howard if you can’t.
    Clay: I’m sure he’d be willing to strike a deal.
    Joyce: Fair enough...
    Joyce: ...
    Joyce: I really did go through all that effort for nothing.
    Clay: Yup.
    do DialogueVars.end_game("Ending Title", "Ending 1/1", Color.GRAY)
- Never mind.
=> END

~ apple
- How are you?
    if DialogueVars.applehow
        Clay: I’m not bothering with that again.  
    else
        Apple: ...
        Apple: ...
        Apple: ...
        Clay: Are you going to say anything, or...?
        Apple: ...
        Clay: Nice talk.
        set DialogueVars.applehow = true
    => apple
- Where is your mom?
    Apple points to the front of the house
    Clay: Figures...
    => apple
- Where were you two nights ago? [if DialogueVars.talked_to_howard1]
    Apple: ...
    Clay: You are determined not to be helpful, huh?
    Apple points at the bank
    Clay: …
    do Music.switch("Secret Jingle")
    Clay: Oh.
    Clay: You were being babysat by Howard again…
    do Music.switch("Nice Day")
    Clay: No one tells me anything.
    set DialogueVars.talked_to_apple = true
    => apple
- Never mind.
=> END

~ seb
- How are you?
    Seb: Well, if you MUST ask, I was on my way home from the checking on the railroad progress.
    Clay: Well, Seb
    Seb: [speed=1.5] please stop calling me that [next=auto]
    Clay: [speed=1.0] I’m glad that you’re keeping yourself busy.
    => seb
- How was work? [if DialogueVars.talked_to_howard2]
    Seb: ...
    Clay: What? Did you not want me to know that you were working?
    Seb: Is maintaining one’s image and status a crime?
    Clay: No, but while you definitely need to keep that a secret to avoid jokes...
    Clay: This is related to a crime, so I need information.
    Clay: Anyways, don’t lie to me again.
    Clay: Understood?
    Seb: Yes sir.
    Clay: Anyways... Did you overhear anything while you were at work?
    Seb: Well, there was a smashing sound and I took a picture.
    Clay: ...
    Seb: ...
    Clay: You took a picture.
    Seb: Yes...?
    Clay: And didn’t TELL ME?!?
    Seb: sorry [next=auto]
    Clay: Just show me the picture.
    Seb: Here it is.
    Clay: ...
    Seb: ...
    Clay: What is this?
    Seb: I know what it looks like...
    Clay: How did you manage to get this blurry of a photo?
    Clay: It looks like an explosion just happened.
    Seb: I tripped, okay!? I couldn’t get better than that.
    Clay: ...
    do Music.switch("Secret Jingle")
    Clay: Wait.
    Clay: There’s a gold ring in their hand.
    do Music.switch("Nice Day")
    Seb: What?
    Clay: Well. It seems you were actually helpful.
    set DialogueVars.talked_to_seb = true
    => seb
- Never mind.
=> END

~ teddy
- How are you?
    Teddy: I am doing wonderful little man.
    Clay: …
    Teddy: What?
    Teddy: Did I say something wrong?
    Clay: You realize you’re just about the only person in this town that could call ME little, right?
    Teddy: Yes, but I feel I should exercise that right.
    Clay: Fine...
    => teddy
- Where were you two nights ago? [if DialogueVars.talked_to_howard1] 
    Teddy: Likely asleep by the fire.
    Clay: ...
    Teddy: I do that a lot.
    Teddy: I’m always tired from the day and the store is closed, so I have nothing to do.
    Clay: You don’t hang out with Harper?
    Teddy: I do when I can, but she is always off in her room.
    Teddy: She stays up way too late studyi-[next=auto]
    Clay: You realize I know Harper, right?
    Clay: We grew up together?
    Teddy: Oh. [wait=1] That’s right!
    Clay: ...
    => teddy
- Never mind.
=> END

~ harper
- How are you? 
    Harper: Tired.
    Clay: More than usual, or just in general?
    Harper: Yep.
    Clay: That didn’t answer the question.
    Harper: I know.
    Clay: ...
    Harper: ...
    Clay: So... [next=auto]
    Harper: Go away.
    Clay: Got it.
    => harper
- Where were you two nights ago? [if DialogueVars.talked_to_howard1] 
    Harper: I was out shooting. What of it?
    Clay: I’m just curious.
    Harper: Well, fix that.
    Clay: Look... I need to know this.
    Harper: What? Are you going to lecture me?
    Harper: Trying to coach my sleep again?
    Clay: I am just trying to verify where you were a couple nights ago. 
    Clay: As long as you have an alibi, I can cross you off the investigation.
    Harper: ...
    Harper: What investigation?
    Clay: Dang...
    Clay: There was a theft at the bank.
    Harper: ...
    Harper: I was at the range for a bit two nights ago.
    Harper: I’ve been testing out some ideas for cartridge primers.
    Harper: I think I’m on the verge of making something replicable.
    Clay: ...
    Clay: That’s amazing!
    Harper: ...
    Clay: Look... I’m happy for you.
    Harper: Thanks...
    => harper
- Never mind.
=> END

